-- title:
--   Decomposition characters on the multiplicative submodule of TₚJ_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, let $M\ge 1$ satisfy $p\mid M$ and $p^2\nmid M$, and let $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ contain every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, and assume the input package [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L113) (the Hecke data at every prime $\ell$ along $H$, and, for each $d\in(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, existence of a diamond automorphism of the base-changed function field of $X_H(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$). Write $J_H(M)$ for the degree-zero divisor class group of that function field and $T=T_p J_H(M)$ for its $p$-adic Tate module, realised as sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$, with its Galois action [`ModularCurve.JH.tateGaloisRep`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L154). Let $\mathbb T$ be a commutative $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra acting on $T$ compatibly with $\mathbb Z_p$ and faithfully, let $op$ assign to each generator $g$ (a $T_\ell$ with $\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid M$; a $U_q$ with $q$ prime, $q\mid M$; or a diamond $\langle d\rangle$) an element of $\mathbb T$ acting as the geometric operator [`ModularCurve.tateGenOpH`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L99), and assume these elements generate $\mathbb T$ as a $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra. Let $S'$ be a splitting datum for $\mathbb T$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ and maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals, with $e_i\in\mathfrak m_j$ iff $i\ne j$), $i_0$ an index, $A=e_{i_0}\mathbb T e_{i_0}$ the corresponding corner ring, $k$ a field of characteristic $p$ and $\pi_k:A\to k$ a ring homomorphism, and let $\bar\theta$ be the induced system of eigenvalues, $\bar\theta(g)=\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,op(g)\,e_{i_0})$; assume the ordinarity condition $\bar\theta(U_p)\ne 0$. Let $\mathrm{Pl}$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ in its nonunits, and let $P^0$ be the $\mathbb T$-submodule of $T$ consisting of the $x$ in the corner submodule $e_{i_0}T$ on which every element $\sigma$ of the inertia subgroup of $\mathrm{Pl}$ over $\mathbb Q$ acts by the scalar $\chi_{\mathrm{cyc},p}(\sigma)\in\mathbb Z_p^\times$. Then there are functions $\chi_1,\chi_2$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $A$, elements $x_0,y\in T$ and an integer $N$ such that: every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $\mathrm{Pl}$ acts on $P^0$ by the scalar $\chi_1(\sigma)$; for every such $\sigma$ and every $x\in e_{i_0}T$ one has $\sigma x-\chi_2(\sigma)\,x\in P^0$; for $\sigma$ in inertia, $\sigma x-x\in P^0$ for all $x\in e_{i_0}T$; and, with $x_0\in P^0$ and $y\in e_{i_0}T$, the pair $(x_0,y)$ is $A$-independent (if $a\,x_0+b\,y=0$ then $a=b=0$), every $z\in e_{i_0}T$ satisfies $p^N z=a\,x_0+b\,y$ for some $a,b\in A$, and every $z\in P^0$ satisfies $p^N z=a\,x_0$ for some $a\in A$.
--
--   This is the local analysis at $p$ of an ordinary corner of the $p$-adic Tate module of $J_H(M)$ when $p$ exactly divides $M$: the multiplicative-type part $P^0$ and the quotient $e_{i_0}T/P^0$ are each generated by one element over the corner ring up to a bounded power of $p$, the decomposition group acts on them by characters $\chi_1,\chi_2$, and inertia acts by the cyclotomic character on $P^0$ and trivially on the quotient. It feeds the construction of the two-dimensional parabolic Galois representation attached to an ordinary non-Eisenstein corner, and of the generator of the multiplicative submodule.
-- source:
